---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../../../components/Hero.astro';
import Cta from '../../../components/Cta.astro';
import SectionNav from '../../../components/SectionNav.astro';
---
<Base title={"Participations and Government Guarantees on a Problem Hotel Loan"} description={"What a community bank should sort out early when a problem hotel loan has participants or a government guarantee: who decides, who must consent, and what to tell a buyer."}>
  <Hero eyebrow="For community banks" title={"Participations and government guarantees."} lead={"Many community-bank hotel loans have participants, a government guarantee, or both. What to sort out early."} />
  <SectionNav section="communityBanks" />
  <main id="main">
<section class="section"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">What we buy</p><h2>Whole loans, participation interests, and guaranteed loans.</h2>
        <p>Whole loans, participation interests, and hotels the bank already owns are all within what we buy. We review government-guaranteed hotel loans and work within the agency's consent requirements for a sale.</p></div>
      <div class="cells two">
        <div><h3>Participations</h3><ul><li>Whether the bank is the lead or a participant</li><li>Who controls decisions on a problem loan under the participation agreement</li><li>What consent a sale needs, and from whom</li><li>What the participants have been told, and when</li><li>Whether the whole loan will be sold, or only the bank's interest</li></ul></div>
        <div><h3>Government guarantees</h3><ul><li>The agency and the percentage guaranteed</li><li>What the guarantee requires of the lender in a default</li><li>Whether the agency's consent is needed for a sale, and how it is obtained</li><li>The status of any claim or demand already made</li></ul></div>
      </div>
      <p class="fine">General points. The participation agreement, the guarantee, and the agency's rules govern, and the bank's counsel should confirm what applies.</p>
    </div></section>

    <section class="section alt"><div class="wrap intro">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Tell us early</p><h2>These belong on the first page.</h2></div>
      <dl class="pillars">
        <div><dt>Under "Participations and guarantees"</dt><dd>On the <a class="more arrow" href="/banks/community-banks/the-loan-summary/">one-page loan summary</a>, say whether there are participants, who is the lead, any government guarantee, and which consents a sale would need.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Why it matters</dt><dd>Consents decide whether a loan sale can close, and how quickly. A buyer prices the time and the risk, so naming them early helps the price.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div></section>

    <section class="section alt"><div class="wrap"><div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">Related reading</p></div><ul class="toc"><li><a href="/glossary/#participation">Participation interest <span>Glossary</span></a></li><li><a href="/glossary/#whole-loan">Whole loan <span>Glossary</span></a></li><li><a href="/banks/faq/">FAQ for banks <span>Banks</span></a></li></ul></div></section>
  </main>
  <Cta title={"Discuss a hotel loan in confidence."} text={"A conversation and an indicative price carry no obligation to sell."} label={"Start a conversation"} />
</Base>
